The schema, as the API sees it:
{
  "$ref": "#/$defs/PaymentBasis",
  "description": "Whether the payment clock starts at the invoice date or at receipt."
}

Extracted 40 of 40 contracts.
Every one is a ContractTerms, not a string.

{
  "supplier": "Voss Industrial",
  "payment_days": 60,
  "payment_basis": "invoice",
  "price_cap_pct": 3,
  "price_notice_days": 30,
  "liability_cap_usd": null
}

Field-level accuracy against the generated ground truth
  payment_days         40/40  100%
  price_cap_pct        40/40  100%
  price_notice_days    40/40  100%
  payment_basis        40/40  100%

  liability_cap_usd is null in 24 of 40 — the contracts
  that state only a percentage. A field that is allowed to be absent is how a
  model says 'not in the document' without inventing something.
